s for a successor because the spec's Context list doesn't name the writer, but \"every reader\" has no exception.\n\n**`RULING: RA-F1 FIX`:** the decoy content is unusual, but the spec names multi-line strings as inside its promise, and the outcome is the same fail-open with data loss. The same fix covers it; it only adds a test case.\n\n**What the fix must do (stdlib has no TOML writer, and re-narrowing the file's shape would undo this lane):**\n- The writer confirms its target through the one parse before rewriting, and refuses, naming the form, when it can't.\n- The flag appliers surface that refusal instead of printing success.\n- Migration keeps the legacy file when the write is refused.\n- The stale docstring goes, and the RESYNC entry qualifies \"any valid TOML\" for the in-place flags and migration.\n\nThe commit hooks passed, including `held-status`, with three readability worsenings in measures that aren't gating. They again said a declared check did not run, so that check didn't grade this commit. The probe's scratch directory and script are under `%TEMP%`, outside the repo."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4044,"cache_read_input_tokens":899628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4044},"output_tokens":759,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"6878a679-45f2-49b6-aece-440226d02bc9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:54:38.412Z","request_id":"req_011CgapfBLrtRy9XoCP9E4ah"}
